        "kind": "text",
        "label": "What the girdle is made of",
        "marks": 0,
        "why": "Each half of the girdle is one bone in the adult, formed from three that fuse at the socket, which is why the socket is where all three meet.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing that the girdle has three bones in all. Each half has three fused parts.",
          "Leaving the sacrum out. The girdle joins the vertebral column at the sacrum."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Ilium above, ischium below, pubis in front — all three meet at the socket.",
        "margin_note": "One short note. The marks are all in the figure.",
        "lines": [
          "The pelvic girdle has two hip bones, one",
          "on each side.",
          "Each hip bone is formed of three fused",
          "bones: ilium, ischium and pubis.",
          "They meet at the socket called the",
          "acetabulum, which holds the femur.",
          "Behind, the girdle joins the sacrum of the",
          "vertebral column."
        ]
